# Test fixtures are vendored from upstream and compared byte for byte, so a
# round-trip test only passes if they check out with the line endings they
# were vendored with. `-text` tells git never to convert them, whatever the
# platform or the user's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Not `text eol=lf`: that means "store LF, check out LF", which is wrong for
# the fixtures that are vendored with CRLF — an EDL is a CRLF format and
# upstream's samples carry it. It also left every clone permanently dirty,
# because git compared the normalized form against blobs that have CRLF.
*.ale -text
*.edl -text
*.otio -text
*.tsv -text

# Structured storage containers, which git must never touch.
*.aaf binary
